+## M19 — External-IdP deployment integration (proposed, unimplemented)
+
+**Status:** NOT_PLANNED. Requirements proposal only; no implementation approval,
+commands or new environment APIs are implied. This does not reopen M00–M13.
+
+**Goal:** permit C1 to be initialized and recovered under an independently managed
+OIDC provider and deployment supervisor without weakening identity, authorization,
+review or recovery safeguards. See `docs/milestones/M19.md` for the integration
+requirements and the existing command capabilities to inspect first.
+
+- **C1-NS8-01:** initialize application and authorization state without creating an
+  IdP realm, users or clients.
+- **C1-NS8-02:** grant first-administrator roles only to an explicitly approved,
+  verified issuer/subject identity; never first login, username/email inference or
+  infrastructure administrator status.
+- **C1-NS8-03:** detect complete and partial initialization and retry without
+  duplicated stores, identity changes or resetting existing application state.
+- **C1-NS8-04:** expose necessary consistency and recovery maintenance through a
+  supported deployment-independent command contract; reuse existing public CLI
+  operations where they already satisfy it, without private imports.
+- **C1-NS8-05:** recover independently of shared IdP data, detect incompatible
+  principal namespaces and retain a verified, explicitly accepted recovery guard.
+
+Packaging may proceed while M19 is pending. Production initialization remains
+blocked until a suitable upstream release implements and verifies these contracts.
+
