+# M19 — External-IdP deployment integration requirements (proposal)
+
+Status: **NOT_PLANNED**. This is a requirements proposal, not an approved
+implementation plan. Baseline inspected: `bcaf67bcefd024d0a14fb5e37c4a0ccd89af0a90`.
+M00–M13 stay completed; M14/M14a work and optional M15–M18 are unchanged.
+
+The requesting deployment is NethServer 8's ns8-cone with the independently
+managed ns8-idp. C1 owns authorization, bootstrap semantics, consistency and
+recovery safeguards. The module owns containers, configuration, routing, domain
+binding, provider registration and backup transport. No packaging runtime patch,
+private import, authentication proxy or replacement administration UI is allowed.
+
+| Requirement | Acceptance condition |
+| --- | --- |
+| C1-NS8-01 external IdP | Initialize C1 knowledge/workflow and authorization state without IdP realm/user/client creation, Keycloak administrator credentials or ownership of Compose |
+| C1-NS8-02 explicit administrator | Verify the intended existing issuer/subject using a supported enrollment contract, record explicit approval, and grant only the required initial roles; reject first-arbitrary-login, username/email inference and infrastructure-admin authority |
+| C1-NS8-03 retry safety | Distinguish clean, partially initialized and complete states; retry after failure without creating duplicate stores/databases, resetting existing grants/content or changing stable instance/IRI/issuer namespace |
+| C1-NS8-04 public maintenance | Qualify existing CLI state/consistency/recovery operations for an externally supervised deployment, with explicit inputs, bounded failures and machine-readable sanitized outputs; request new functionality only for demonstrated gaps |
+| C1-NS8-05 external recovery | Restore knowledge/workflow and authorization persistence independently of shared IdP backups; preserve stable application identity, reject incompatible issuer/subject namespaces and keep publication guarded until verification and explicit security-snapshot acceptance |
+
+## Reuse existing capabilities first
+
+Inspect the public CLI operations `c1-admin internal state`, `consistency`,
+`guard-set`, `dr-verify` and `dr-release` before adding equivalents. They are
+existing command names at this baseline, but have not been qualified for NS8.
+The reference host backup stops its single writer and TerminusDB to export
+storage, dumps OpenFGA and private Keycloak databases, and creates checksums.
+Retain supported backend consistency procedures and the C1 guard semantics;
+allow the deployment supervisor to supply a consistent backup set without
+requiring ownership of Keycloak or reference networking.
+
+The baseline internal bootstrap creates the private realm and user and rejects
+an existing realm. It does not satisfy external enrollment or initialization retry
+safety. Do not extract its private internals into packaging or weaken token
+validation: issuer, audience, signature, expiry, access-token purpose and required
+`c1_principal_kind` remain mandatory. The shared provider supplies a constrained
+`human` claim for user-authorized clients.
+
+## Required verification in the later implementation plan
+
+Clean initialization with an existing external provider; explicit identity
+verification and wrong-issuer/subject rejection; retry after each durable partial
+step; idempotent complete retry; namespace mismatch; preserved store/model and
+instance identity; integrity/consistency failures; corrupt/partial backup; guarded
+restore onto another infrastructure instance; failed and successful guard release
+with explicit acceptance; permission revocations and independent-review behavior.
+Use real C1, backends and provider. Do not mark mock checks as interoperability.
+
+No command name, new configuration variable or verification receipt format is
+proposed here. Define those contracts in a separately approved implementation
+plan, and ship them upstream before production packaging enables initialization.
